# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Sanity-tested once on 2026-11-13 (one ingest, one compile, two questions) on a paid
# Gemini key. Not load-tested; the free-tier notes below are from documentation.
#
# Backend settings for the mixed preset of the LiteLLM gateway: chat on the
# host's Ollama, embeddings on Gemini (docker-compose.litellm.yml with
# deploy/litellm/mixed.yaml).
#
# In .env, replace the model settings from .env.example (DEFAULT_MODELS_*,
# REASONING_*, NON_REASONING_*, EMBED_*, RERANK_*) with these lines, then:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.litellm.yml up -d
#
# Every triplet is set in full, so no field falls back to a built-in NVIDIA
# endpoint. Model names are the gateway aliases from mixed.yaml. URLs use the
# in-network name "litellm"; for a backend run on the host (uv run ...), use
# http://127.0.0.1:4000 instead. Docker Compose and the backend's .env loader
# both expand ${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}; another loader may need the key written out.
#
# Chat stays on this machine. Catalog text for embedding goes to Google, and
# Google's pricing page says free-tier content is used to improve its
# products; paid-tier content is not.

# --- Gateway ---
LITELLM_PRESET=mixed
# The gateway's only credential; the backend sends it as its API key below.
# Required: Compose refuses to start the gateway while this is empty. Set a
# long random value, e.g. the output of: echo "sk-$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
# Used by the gateway only. The backend containers load .env too but do not
# read it. Create one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Limits apply per
# Google Cloud project, not per key.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Chat ---
# The gateway speaks the OpenAI protocol, so both roles use the OpenAI-style
# client whatever the model is called.
REASONING_ENDPOINT=http://litellm:4000/v1
REASONING_API_KEY=${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}
REASONING_MODEL=ao-chat
REASONING_CLIENT=openai

NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=http://litellm:4000/v1
NON_REASONING_API_KEY=${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}
NON_REASONING_MODEL=ao-chat
NON_REASONING_CLIENT=openai

# Same as env.ollama.example: turns thinking off on qwen3.5. Measured through
# the gateway: about 0.2 s and 2 tokens for a one-word answer with it, 3-4 s
# and 120-150 tokens without.
LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=none

# Same as env.ollama.example. A single local GPU is slow and serves one request
# at a time; these are the values the tested Ollama run used.
LLM_INVOKE_TIMEOUT_S=600
LLM_MAX_INFLIGHT=2
SEMANTIC_LLM_MAX_INFLIGHT=2

# --- Embeddings ---
# The backend appends /embeddings to this URL itself.
EMBED_ENDPOINT=http://litellm:4000/v1
EMBED_API_KEY=${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}
EMBED_MODEL=ao-embed
# mixed.yaml asks gemini-embedding-001 for 768 dimensions. The two must
# match. Ingest and query must use the same model.
EMBED_DIMENSIONS=768
# Same as env.gemini.example. Free tier: about 100 requests and 30,000 input
# tokens a minute (third-party figures, unverified). With 10 texts per request
# and one request at a time per embedding call, a single request fits in one
# minute's quota even if every text counts as a request and hits the
# 2,048-token input limit. A long ingest still goes over and relies on the
# backend's chunk retries. Each call has its own limit, so parallel ingests
# add up. On a paid tier, remove both lines (upstream: 32 and 32).
EMBED_BATCH_SIZE=10
EMBED_MAX_CONCURRENT=1

# --- Rerank ---
# No rerank model in mixed.yaml, so rerank is off. "disabled" sends no
# request: the only caller, bridge-table owner selection, takes the first
# candidate Term. To enable it, add an ao-rerank model to the gateway config
# and set RERANK_ENDPOINT=http://litellm:4000/rerank.
RERANK_ENDPOINT=disabled
RERANK_API_KEY=${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}
RERANK_MODEL=ao-rerank
